ory reaper killed the run. That is environment, not code.\n\n| # | Failing test(s) | Evidence | Class | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | charge-analysis CI-A18, CI-A19, flag-off, CI-U04, CI-A21, plus the afterAll flag reset (step 6) | 401 starts at the first mid-file `reseed()`, which recreates the seed users. The file ran 49 s, so the 600 s token lifetime is not the cause | test design | New `signIn()` logs everyone in again in beforeAll and after each mid-test reseed |\n| 2 | DD-E01 (dd-api) | The only event was the platform's normal `authz.denied` for a 403, not a dd action | test design (assertion too broad) | Now asserts no `dd_*` event and exactly that one `authz.denied` with its metadata (stricter) |\n| 3 | DD-X01 (dd-audit) | Comparing against seeded `CLM-HOSTILE-*` numbers gave NaN. Every product assertion before that line passed | test design | Only `^CLM-\\d{4,}$` numbers are compared, read across all pages |\n| 4 | DD-X02, X03, X04, X05, X09 | \"DD-X01 did not run\" | cascade of #3 | none |\n| 5 | dev-flags T-FLAG-05 and T-FLAG-11 (step 4) | Expected 3 flags; there are 7 now | test design (stale pin) | Count now equals the 7 registry keys (additive) |\n| 6 | fuel-api CI-A06 | The archive event carries version 2. The step-7 contract does not say whether it is the pre- or post-archive version | test design | Pinned to the stored archived row version, asserted to be 2 |\n| 7 | fuel-api CI-A13 | VIEWER gets 403 on document detail | test design | Uses ANALYST, as the step-5/6 suites do |\n| 8 | fuel-api CI-A15 | Bulk `limit: 100` is refused; the maximum is 25 | test design | limit 25 |\n| 9 | fuel-db CI-D01 | The policy regex looked for `app.tenant_id`; the policies use `fr_current_tenant()` | test design | Matches `tenant_id = fr_current_tenant()` on both USING and WITH CHECK (stricter) |\n| 10 | fuel-db CI-D03 | Baseline insert failed: `updated_by_id` is NOT NULL and the insert helper filled a random uuid | test design | Baselines and the cross-tenant probe now set `updated_by_id`, so only the intended violation can make an insert fail |\n\nI also checked the builder's integration findings (`claims.read` scope name, reject body without `acknowledgePendingFindings`, invoice page size 50, 7 flags) against my acceptance files; they are already correct there.\n\n**Light checks:** eslint is clean on all touched files, and `tsc -p api/tsconfig.json` exits 0.\n\n**Needs the database rerun:**\n- the 39 api files that never started, including dd-db and the step 5–8 Tier H files\n- the 6 fixed files: charge-analysis, dd-api, dd-audit, dev-flags, fuel-api, fuel-db\n- the web Tier H tests\n\nTo stay under the memory limit, run the api files in batches of 8–10 with `npx vitest run --project acceptance --maxWorkers=1 <files>`.\n\nFiles changed (all under `api/test-acceptance/`): charge-analysis.acc.test.ts, dd-api.acc.test.ts, dd-audit.acc.test.ts, dev-flags.acc.test.ts, fuel-api.acc.test.ts, fuel-db.acc.test.ts.\n\nFiles are in C:/Users/mariu/.[REDACTED:high_entropy]:\n- test-plan.md (classification section appended)\n- mailbox.md (appended)","s":true},"signals":{"tool_error":5},"tainted_tools":1,"n_tool_calls":253,"scrub_hits":{"high_entropy":10}}